        "original_id": "978b6b1c-ee92-504b-88d1-370adfc7d570",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: The Happiest Millionaire, Mars Needs Moms, Fortuosity, A Christmas Carol\n- Companies: The Walt Disney Company, ImageMovers, ImageMovers Digital, The Walt Disney Studios\n- People: Fred MacMurray, Anthony J. Drexel Biddle, Berkeley Breathed\n\nFacts:\n- The Happiest Millionaire is a 1967 musical film starring Fred MacMurray and based on the true story of Anthony J. Drexel Biddle, a Philadelphia millionaire.\n- Fortuosity is the first song in the 1967 motion picture The Happiest Millionaire.\n- From 2007 to 2010, The Walt Disney Company and ImageMovers operated the joint animation facility ImageMovers Digital.\n- ImageMovers Digital produced the performance-captured animated films A Christmas Carol and Mars Needs Moms for The Walt Disney Studios.\n- Mars Needs Moms is a 2011 American computer-animated film based on Berkeley Breathed's book of the same title.",
